Lists all available projects in `motion-projects`, their title, aspect ratio (16x9, 9x16, 1x1, 4x5), frame rate, duration in seconds, scene count, and associated cues or storyboard files. (27 October 2026)

### Render a Motion Design project (27 October 2026)

```bash
# Render to MP4 with native format
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-motion.mjs --render macbook-pro-s20-fingerprint-ppm --out output.mp4

# Render with format override to 1:1 square at 60 fps
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-motion.mjs --render macbook-pro-s20-fingerprint-ppm --format 1x1 --fps 60 --out /tmp/thumb.mp4

# Render to PNG sequence
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-motion.mjs --render macbook-pro-s20-fingerprint-ppm --output-format png-sequence --out /tmp/frames
```

The script cooks the project into a temporary HyperFrames bundle, adjusting format and frame rate if overridden, then invokes the pinned private wrapper `RunHyperframes.mjs render` using headless Chrome. (27 October 2026)

### Assemble a 1:1 Montage (27 October 2026)

```bash
# Run full montage build (plan, audio, video, mov, verify, index)
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-motion.mjs --montage /path/to/Params/montage.json

# Run a specific sub-step
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-motion.mjs --montage /path/to/Params/montage.json --step audio
```

Calls `Montage.py` from the template or local workshop, running the single pass ffmpeg pipeline, QuickTime MOV container copy, 35 point verification, and index generation. (27 October 2026)

## 2. SFX CLI: zenray-edit-sfx.mjs (27 October 2026)

Script location:
`/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-sfx.mjs`

### List SFX library and reference recipes (27 October 2026)

```bash
# Formatted table
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-sfx.mjs --list

# Raw JSON
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-sfx.mjs --list --json
```

Scans reference reproductions in `out/repro-03/` with their recipes and invariance scores, sound archetypes in `params/archetypes.json`, designed film proposals in `params/proposals/`, and motion bank sounds. (27 October 2026)

### Normalize and master audio (27 October 2026)

```bash
# Master to standard -14 LUFS with -1.5 dBFS ceiling
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-sfx.mjs --normalize input.wav --out output.wav

# Custom loudness target and ceiling
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-sfx.mjs --normalize input.wav --out output.wav --target-lufs -16.0 --ceiling -2.0
```

Applies the mastering chain: 20 Hz high-pass filter, constant volume gain to target loudness, and look-ahead limiter (`alimiter=limit=<ceiling>:attack=5:release=60:level=disabled`). An iterative loop refines the gain until measured loudness converges within 0.1 LU of the target. (27 October 2026)

### Link SFX to video clips or Motion Design projects (27 October 2026)

```bash
# Link sound to a montage clip via chain.json (schema zenray-edit/chain@1)
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-sfx.mjs --link --video Sources/clip1.mp4 --sfx sfx:repro/12-Denied --out chain.json --cue lens --offset 15

# Bind sound to a Motion Design project via sfx.json (schema zenray-sfx-binding/1)
node /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/scripts/zenray-edit-sfx.mjs --link --video motion:zenray-logo-opening-ppm --sfx sfx:repro/12-Denied --out /path/to/project/sfx.json --cue lens --offset 20
```

Automatically detects the target format:
- `chain.json`: single clip montage binding with video path, sfx reference, anchor cue or timestamp, offset in milliseconds, and gain in dB.
- `sfx.json`: multi-track motion project sidecar with schema `zenray-sfx-binding/1`, appending new tracks and preserving immutable revision history. (27 October 2026)

